WEBVTT

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.900
<i>Are you adventurers,</i>

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.440
<i>who seek the true form of the mythical being</i>

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:13.040
<i>that dwells deep beyond the waterfalls named Perilous?</i>

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.100
<i>If you are, you must first find me.</i>

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:35.090
<i>The year was 1889.</i>

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>In the Atlantic Ocean,
ship after ship met with mysterious accidents.</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.330
<i>People laid the blame on monsters</i>

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.760
<i>which had lived in the seas from ancient times.</i>

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.270
<i>The world powers accused each other</i>

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:48.060
<i>of attacks using new weapons.</i>

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.700
<i>It was a time of dangerous buildup of military tension.</i>

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:54.650
<i>Heavy industries, led by steel mills, were expanding,</i>

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:56.810
<i>and foreign trade was growing.</i>

00:00:56.810 --> 00:01:01.830
<i>The world powers growled over colonies in Asia and Africa.</i>

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:04.390
<i>There were repeated military clashes.</i>

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.630
<i>Towards the end of the 19th Century,</i>

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:09.630
<i>civilization prospered, but the people cowered with fear</i>

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:12.460
<i>as the threat of a world war loomed ever closer.</i>

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:04.700
Paris... Paris...

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:24.300
It's the Eiffel Tower!

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.240
What a terrific sight!

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:38.810
So this is the Paris Exposition!

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:47.520
There is still a one hour waiting time.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:49.740
Don't push! Please, don't push!

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:52.020
Amazing!

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:57.250
Wow! How cool!

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.250
But they're not ready to fly.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:07.260
It sure is big! But there's too much loss in the drive system.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:12.260
It feels like we've come more to see people than inventions.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.520
Darn it! The contest is about to start!

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:23.690
The First International Flying Competition will now begin.

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:27.490
This competition will be for flight distance.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:31.860
The winner will receive a cash prize of 20,000 francs!

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:34.190
Uncle!

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:37.490
Hey, Jean, I was waiting for you!

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:38.500
Sorry to be late.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:39.670
Is that so?

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:42.540
Look over there! Number 1 aircraft is getting ready to take off.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.040
What do you think about that one?

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:48.260
Those wings won't support the engine.

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:54.880
Wind force two... with the wind eight meters.

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:58.890
Really? If so, that one's going to crash.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:11.360
The flight distance for Number 1 was eight meters.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:12.860
Just as we thought!

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:15.700
Next, the Number 2 craft.

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:19.470
This aircraft has been flown over Dover in England.

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:22.600
Lord Arkwright, if you please?

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:33.880
Too bad, Lord!

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:36.390
Uncle, when's our turn?

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:40.030
Sorry, Jean. I drew Number 102.

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:41.300
It'll be evening then.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:42.760
I guess so.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:46.600
It's still early, but let's take the aircraft out of the boat, okay?

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:47.400
Sure.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:04.550
You didn't get seasick on the way over, did you?

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:06.420
Just a little.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:08.920
I see, well, that's good to hear.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:12.760
You got a lot of work done even though you were on the boat.

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:13.690
Yeah.

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:17.200
Sorry about that, but you know I can't stand ships.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:19.800
Don't worry about it.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:24.560
Speaking of ships, I'm told that America ordered her new battleship

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:26.560
to hunt down the sea monsters.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:30.010
You lost your father to them.

00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:32.570
His death hasn't been confirmed yet.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:36.480
Yeah, that's right.

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:39.290
Number 22, the Pierre!

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:41.240
The top contender!

00:06:43.990 --> 00:06:46.290
That's the top contender?

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:47.710
It looks like the prize is ours.

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:50.710
So it seems, and by a wide margin too!

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.260
You think so too?

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:57.500
That 20,000 francs is ours!

00:06:57.500 --> 00:07:01.340
Now we can really start inventing.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:04.380
My old lady won't be able to complain.

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:08.730
But before that, we're going to have lots of fun in Paris!

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:16.190
We could go look for your father,

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:19.990
but you could go looking for a girlfriend too.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:27.080
Now, Jean, we only live once! We've got to make the most of it!

00:07:37.670 --> 00:07:40.300
Hey, Jean, hand me that wrench, will you?

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:44.320
Well, what's the matter?

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:45.890
Uncle, I have to go!

00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:47.810
Hey, what about the 20,000 francs?

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:49.860
I haven't forgotten!

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:52.190
I'll be back by evening!

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:56.320
20,000 francs!

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:59.360
I've found her at last.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.100
It's her all right.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:04.270
You guys better not lose her!

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:05.030
Right!

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:09.120
Looks like she's headed for the Eiffel Tower.

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:37.790
France, Spain, ltaly, Egypt, Africa...

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:42.680
Say, King, I wonder where I was born?

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:45.280
Africa, the same as you?

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:50.830
But you wouldn't know either, would you?

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:55.080
Yeah...

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:57.990
If we could only fly, we could go searching.

00:08:57.990 --> 00:08:59.460
You can fly!

00:09:03.590 --> 00:09:07.010
I'm Jean, Jean Rocque Raltique.

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:09.520
I'm the boy who can take you through the skies.

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:15.400
What's wrong? Don't you believe me?

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:17.740
We can really fly!

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:21.550
I came from Le Havre to compete in the flying competition.

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:23.650
Where did you come from?

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:25.740
Wait, let me guess...

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:27.890
India?

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:28.910
It's not India?

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:34.120
I'm sorry, but I don't know a thing about you. So why should I...

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.630
Good! You answered me.

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:40.000
I thought maybe you couldn't understand me.

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:43.260
Look, I'm sorry if I said something wrong.

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:47.510
You're lying! My dark skin must look funny to you.

00:09:47.510 --> 00:09:49.220
That's not true!

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:53.640
I wonder. Well then, what do you want with me?

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:57.450
We happen to be in Paris at the same time.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:00.190
I thought how nice it would be if we could be friends!

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:01.500
No, thank you.

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:09.240
Funny looking cat.

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:10.410
He's a lion.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:18.170
Now, don't keep looking so grim.

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:23.420
We only live once, you know! We've got to make the most of it!

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:32.220
What is this? It's an amazing invention.

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:37.220
King, let's go.

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:43.030
That's enough. Stop making such a scene in public.

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:46.400
I've been watching you for so long, so long now!

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:49.570
Don't be so hard on the kid, Ms. Grandis.

00:10:50.030 --> 00:10:53.040
Yeah, let's get down to business first.

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:57.790
You two shut up! Give me that blue glass bauble this instant.

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:05.510
We've searched all over Europe looking for you and that bauble.

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:08.390
Hurry up now!

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:09.880
Or else!

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:14.260
Put those away, please. She's only a small child.

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:15.730
Right!

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:16.940
Hurry up and hand it over.

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:20.270
Never!

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:21.460
Is that so?

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:22.570
Sanson!

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:22.580
Anytime!
Sanson!

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:23.040
Anytime!

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:23.800
Hanson!

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:24.970
Ready!

00:11:24.970 --> 00:11:26.070
Take care of her.

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:26.780
Yes, Ma'am!

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:29.990
She jumped!

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:37.040
After them!

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:00.600
Goodbye.

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:10.050
That was...

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:11.030
...amazing!

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:13.920
What's wrong with you? She got away!

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:17.160
Oh well, we know where she's headed.

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:19.660
We do? Where's that?

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:24.970
The way she moved and that funny looking cat should make it clear.

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:28.300
Change of plans. Let's get out of here before anyone comes.

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:29.770
Right!

00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:34.200
Like an acrobat and that funny cat...

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:36.430
Lion...

00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:38.640
That's it! They're from a circus!

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:54.930
Mister, when does the show start?

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:57.120
Oh, very soon.

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:00.790
What a relief! She's okay!

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:18.100
It's show time. Change into your costume.

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:22.100
Master, I don't feel like performing today.

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:25.100
If I do, I feel that something evil is going to happen.

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:26.860
I can't allow that!

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:30.360
You had your breakfast this morning, didn't you?

00:13:31.570 --> 00:13:32.360
Yes.

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:35.370
Then you have to earn it by working.

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:38.790
I understand.

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:42.620
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:47.210
Thank you for waiting!

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:50.880
And now, may I introduce to you

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:53.170
Jungle Dancer, Princess Nadia!

00:13:57.390 --> 00:14:00.180
I see! So her name is Nadia!

00:14:14.530 --> 00:14:15.360
Now, remember.

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:19.530
No more rough stuff.

00:14:19.530 --> 00:14:22.420
We're going to talk quietly and legally.

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:23.160
Right.

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:26.750
But what's legal about phoney money?

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:28.670
You talk too much!

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:34.170
Circus master!

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:37.720
There's something I want to talk to you about.

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:40.830
Chotomess!

00:14:43.720 --> 00:14:45.730
Seti! Neferto!

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:05.080
Up!

00:15:13.340 --> 00:15:16.800
That calls for a big round of applause!

00:15:21.510 --> 00:15:23.260
She's wonderful!

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:25.780
That was Princess Nadia!

00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:48.920
Bonjour, mademoiselle.

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:56.050
What's the matter? She's your sister, isn't she?

00:15:57.420 --> 00:16:00.180
Yes, I am. I'm Grandis Granba.

00:16:02.300 --> 00:16:06.560
I've looked all over for you, Nadia.
Now, let's go home.

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:14.030
Every girl likes flowers.

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:16.860
No, let me go! No!

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:20.270
It's no use struggling and making a fuss!

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:23.240
I'm your legal guardian, aren't l?

00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:26.740
Look, I've paid for your keep up to now.

00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:27.750
Master, please!

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:29.540
That's the way it is!

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:37.260
Now, shall we go?

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:39.210
Nadia!

00:16:48.390 --> 00:16:50.000
Wait for me!

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:53.630
I tried to be nice to her and see what happens!

00:16:53.630 --> 00:16:56.020
Now we use force!

00:16:56.020 --> 00:16:57.780
You got it!

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:02.640
Hey, Nadia! Nadia, listen to me.

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:05.780
Those three are after you, right?
I'll help you get away!

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:08.080
I can get away by myself!

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:12.540
Don't call me Nadia so casually. I'm not on display anymore!

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:21.590
Don't be so hardheaded.

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:23.130
Get on!

00:17:25.970 --> 00:17:28.800
Why do those three want that stone so badly?

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:30.430
Is it so valuable?

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:35.810
You don't have to say if you don't want to.

00:17:36.230 --> 00:17:37.110
Where are they?

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:39.670
Don't worry. They can't catch us on foot.

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:47.120
Amazing! An iron covered wagon? I wonder who invented that?

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.330
That would be me!

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:54.250
You can't get away now. Come over here before you get hurt!

00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:57.210
So that's your answer.

00:17:57.790 --> 00:17:58.770
Let them have it!

00:17:58.770 --> 00:17:59.710
Okay, here we go.

00:18:00.130 --> 00:18:03.220
You're going to see what happens when you disobey your elders!

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:08.270
You think you can get away on a toy like that?

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:09.850
I'll show you! Okay, Ma'am?

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:11.720
Sure, go ahead.

00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:12.650
Hanson!

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:14.270
I know what to do.

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:25.030
Nadia!

00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:28.760
What's this? Hey, stop this! It's dangerous!

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:32.100
You brat, that's what you get for meddling.

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:34.900
Get a little sense in your head!

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:45.810
Before anyone comes, let's switch to flight mode.

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:46.470
Yes, Ma'am!

00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:49.930
Geez, I almost got killed!

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:03.320
Wait!

00:19:03.320 --> 00:19:05.330
Geez, he won't give up.

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:06.320
What shall we do?

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:10.530
Let him go. We've got the Blue Water now.

00:19:10.530 --> 00:19:13.040
Goodbye! Adios!

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:14.250
Sayonara!

00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:31.850
Where's that Jean?

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:33.970
Uncle!

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:36.260
Hey, I've been waiting for you!

00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:37.850
Is it ready to fly?

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:44.400
Can't you go a little faster?

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:46.070
We're flying at top speed already.

00:19:46.070 --> 00:19:49.530
It would have been faster traveling on the ground.

00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:53.530
Number 99, the Hinomoto craft!

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:55.580
What is this? You're out of turn!

00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:00.370
Jean!

00:20:00.370 --> 00:20:01.130
Come on, climb!

00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:07.590
That's the way!

00:20:07.860 --> 00:20:09.330
This feels great!

00:20:15.890 --> 00:20:16.640
There it is!

00:20:16.640 --> 00:20:19.330
We'll head straight for Dover.

00:20:20.060 --> 00:20:23.400
Farewell, my lovely city of flowers!

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:24.940
Nadia!

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:28.400
Wait a moment! I'm coming to your rescue!

00:20:30.070 --> 00:20:30.910
Look out!

00:20:33.990 --> 00:20:35.490
Get out of my way!

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:44.630
What was that?

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:50.880
What are you doing?

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:56.600
Nadia, are you all right?

00:20:57.100 --> 00:20:59.180
Yes, but I can't get these things off.

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:02.190
Wait a second. Oh, they're made of paper.

00:21:03.230 --> 00:21:05.250
Do something about this cat!

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:06.820
It's a lion!

00:21:07.730 --> 00:21:09.110
I'll show you!

00:21:14.950 --> 00:21:16.530
Thank you!

00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:19.460
Stop!

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:30.640
Look, I'm not ready to die in a crash yet.

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:33.090
Don't worry. We have the Seine below us.

00:21:34.010 --> 00:21:36.820
Those kids are pretty good.

00:21:36.820 --> 00:21:39.720
But I'll never give up!

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:41.640
That Blue Water will be mine!

00:21:55.840 --> 00:21:59.950
They can't come after us on water. Let's get away on this boat.

00:22:13.050 --> 00:22:14.650
Are you cold?

00:22:17.340 --> 00:22:20.010
No. What's your name?

00:22:20.010 --> 00:22:22.220
What? Haven't I told you yet?

00:22:22.220 --> 00:22:24.230
I'm sorry. I guess I forgot.

00:22:24.230 --> 00:22:26.870
You shouldn't forget me. Jean! I'm Jean!

00:22:26.870 --> 00:22:30.060
Thank you, Jean, for rescuing me.

00:22:33.860 --> 00:22:37.200
Where will you go now? Back to the circus?

00:22:39.530 --> 00:22:41.660
I can't go back.

00:22:41.660 --> 00:22:43.280
What about your folks?

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:45.980
I don't have any.

00:22:47.710 --> 00:22:49.320
I see.

00:22:49.960 --> 00:22:52.300
It's the same with me.

00:22:54.510 --> 00:22:56.930
Say, why don't you come to Le Havre with me!

00:22:57.130 --> 00:22:59.680
I have an uncle there.

00:22:59.680 --> 00:23:01.970
Uncle and Auntie are both very nice.

00:23:01.970 --> 00:23:03.840
I'm sure they'll be glad to help us.

00:23:03.840 --> 00:23:05.680
Hey!

00:23:05.680 --> 00:23:08.000
Hey, Jean!

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:10.690
Uncle!

00:23:10.690 --> 00:23:13.550
Look at this, Jean! It's a special prize!

00:23:13.550 --> 00:23:15.950
We were not an official participant, so no prize money.

00:23:15.950 --> 00:23:19.350
That's wonderful! We'll go on ahead.

00:23:19.350 --> 00:23:20.820
Okay.

